SPLIT R:RULE-M1-0139 | a: Reserved decisions require explicit approval. | b: Changing an accepted project or architecture decision, including a capability selection, is Reserved. | c: Adopting a new architectural style or pattern (CQRS, mediator, Vertical Slice Architecture, event sourcing, microservices, Rich Domain Model or systematic DDD tactical patterns, project-wide Result model) is Reserved. | d: Adding a production project, layer or assembly is Reserved. | e: Changing persistence boundaries (including multiple contexts) or persistence technology is Reserved. | f: Adding a messaging, background processing or distributed caching infrastructure category is Reserved. | g: Adding a search, external storage or external identity infrastructure category is Reserved. | h: Adding a major library or framework is Reserved. | i: Replacing an approved baseline technology is Reserved. | j: Introducing a project-wide convention or abstraction is Reserved. | k: Changing the authentication/authorization architecture is Reserved. | l: Making a breaking public API change is Reserved.
